<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ⚠ GUIDANCE FOR HOST APPS — THIS FILE IS NOT WIRED, AND DELIBERATELY SO.

  We do NOT set `android:fullBackupContent` (or `android:dataExtractionRules`)
  in the SDK's own AndroidManifest.xml, because a LIBRARY manifest declaring
  either attribute produces a manifest-merger CONFLICT for every host app that
  declares its own — the build fails with "Attribute application@
  fullBackupContent ... is also present at ..." and the app author has to add
  `tools:replace`. Shipping that in a library upgrade would break customers'
  builds, which is a worse outcome than the thing it protects against.

  ⚠ WHAT THE ACTUAL EXPOSURE IS, STATED HONESTLY. Sendora's auth tokens live in
  `EncryptedSharedPreferences` (file `sendora_sdk_secure`) under an Android
  Keystore master key. Keystore keys are non-exportable and are NOT backed up.
  So if these prefs DO ride a cloud backup to a new device, the restored blob is
  UNDECRYPTABLE — the failure is a lost session, not a leaked credential. That
  is a real annoyance and is not a security hole, which is why this is guidance
  rather than something we force.

  ⚠ Sendora's own storage fails CLOSED: if `EncryptedSharedPreferences` cannot
  initialise, `Storage.kt` refuses to persist tokens rather than falling back to
  plaintext, and logs why. There is no plaintext copy of a token to back up.

  TO EXCLUDE THEM ANYWAY (recommended — it turns a confusing restored-but-broken
  session into a clean signed-out one), merge these entries into your own rules
  and point your manifest at them:

      <application
          android:fullBackupContent="@xml/your_backup_rules"
          android:dataExtractionRules="@xml/your_extraction_rules"
          tools:replace="android:fullBackupContent" />

  Android 12+ (API 31) reads `dataExtractionRules`; earlier reads
  `fullBackupContent`. Ship both if you support both.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="sendora_sdk.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="sendora_sdk_secure.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
